-- The same dead-argument reduction reached through a *named* top-level
-- function rather than a directly-applied lambda (so ModalityInfer types the
-- node via `applyI`, not the let rule), and with a Bool-typed intractable
-- argument rather than a Float one -- the argument's return type is as
-- irrelevant as its distribution when nothing reads it. Companion to
-- deadBindingIntractable.ppl.
ignoreArg x = Normal
main = ignoreArg ((Uniform * Uniform) > 0.5)
